# env
#
# Deliberately broad. `.env*.local` only matches names ENDING in .local, so a
# `.env.local.bak` written by an editor, a script, or a careful person about to
# change something was committable, and it holds every key the project has. One
# rule that covers every variant, with the template explicitly exempted.
.env*
!.env.example

# vercel
.vercel

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# logs
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# Reference images that fed the analyst's column illustrations, retired on
# 25 September 2026. The folder still holds about 25 MB of local PNGs that were
# never meant for the repo, so it stays ignored: without this line the next
# `git add -A` would commit them to a public repository.
assets/refs/
